IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sca-spent`
IMPORT `sca-qa`

-- Spent Convictions Act 1988 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (sca-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and
-- every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error. Each
-- question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with the value under which the situation does not
-- hold (FALSE) and every later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise for you`. Every situation input is a
-- BOOLEAN, so the trap of graffiti finding 31 cannot hide a read of it.
--
-- For the person convicted or charged (the baseline's seat), each case is asserted twice: once against a value worked
-- by hand from the text (taken from the baseline's own cases, sca-cases-spent.l4, with the life's event ids), and once
-- against the baseline export's own answer on the same facts, carried into the layer's answer type. For the employer or
-- other person, the values are worked by hand from the text.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `an unasked conviction` IS A `My conviction`
ASSUME `an unasked matter` IS A `My matter`
ASSUME `an unasked Schedule 3 role` IS A `My role`
ASSUME `an unasked source` IS A `Where the question comes from`
ASSUME `an unasked use` IS A `How a law of Western Australia uses my record`
ASSUME `an unasked treater` IS A `Who is treating me less favourably`
ASSUME `an unasked relation` IS A `What I am to the person`
ASSUME `an unasked question source` IS A `Where my question comes from`

`as the person convicted or charged` MEANS `I was convicted of an offence, or charged with one`
`as the employer or other person dealing with them` MEANS `I employ, engage, license or deal with someone who has an old conviction or charge`

-- The baseline's fixtures (sca-cases-spent.l4), with the same facts.

